## Exact binary64 host mathematics, with identical non-NaN bits at runtime and
## comptime on JVM, native and wasm. Each primitive rounds to nearest even once;
## integer rounding preserves signed zero. No dynamic rounding mode is exposed.
#
# Backends own only the six exact operations. Classification and scaling stay
# here over the raw-bit pair, so a libm's NaN-ignoring min/max or intermediate
# underflow cannot change the public contract. The constants below are frozen
# MPFR round-to-nearest binary64 patterns, independent of decimal parsing.

# Translated and modified from Netlib fdlibm 5.3. Distinct source notices
# follow verbatim (the comment marker is the only formatting change).

